        "original_id": "b634573d-9b15-5645-b115-f52b01481db3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Parsifal, Manon\n- People: Richard Wagner, Jules Massenet, Henri Meilhac, Philippe Gille, Abbé Prévost, Emil Scaria\n- Places: Bayreuth\n- Roles: Gurnemanz\n\nFacts:\n- In 1731, Abbé Prévost wrote the novel \"L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.\"\n- In 1882, Emil Scaria created the role of Gurnemanz in \"Parsifal\" for Richard Wagner at Bayreuth.\n- \"Parsifal\" is a three-act opera by German composer Richard Wagner.\n- \"Manon\" is an opéra comique in five acts by Jules Massenet.\n- \"Manon\" has a French libretto by Henri Meilhac and Philippe Gille.\n- \"Manon\" is based on Abbé Prévost’s 1731 novel \"L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
